{"alignments": [{"id": "PSA.29.10.a001", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.29.10.001"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.29.10.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001"], "target_head": "t001"}, {"id": "PSA.29.10.a002", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.29.10.005"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.29.10.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t002"], "target_head": "t002"}, {"id": "PSA.29.10.a003", "note": "Italic *as King* in the first colon answers to no morpheme there; the Hebrew writes מֶלֶךְ only in the second colon, after this clause, so rule 25's resumption does not reach back to it. One `added` unit under rule 2. Competing reading: a discontinuous unit on s009 holding both *as King*s.", "source": [], "source_head": null, "status": "added", "target": ["t003", "t004"], "target_head": "t004"}, {"id": "PSA.29.10.a004", "note": "לְ rendered temporally as *at*.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.29.10.002"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.29.10.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t005"], "target_head": "t005"}, {"id": "PSA.29.10.a005", "note": "Assimilated article takes the written *the* (rule 12).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.29.10.003"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.29.10.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t006"], "target_head": "t006"}, {"id": "PSA.29.10.a006", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.29.10.004"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.29.10.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t007"], "target_head": "t007"}, {"id": "PSA.29.10.a007", "note": "Waw rendered *Yea* (rule 14).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.29.10.006"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.29.10.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t008"], "target_head": "t008"}, {"id": "PSA.29.10.a008", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.29.10.007"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.29.10.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t010"], "target_head": "t010"}, {"id": "PSA.29.10.a009", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.29.10.008"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.29.10.008", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t009"], "target_head": "t009"}, {"id": "PSA.29.10.a010", "note": "Bare predicate nominal; the supplied *as* belongs to the noun whose case-function licenses it (rule 33).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.29.10.009"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.29.10.009", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t011", "t012"], "target_head": "t012"}, {"id": "PSA.29.10.a011", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.29.10.010"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.29.10.010", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t013"], "target_head": "t013"}, {"id": "PSA.29.10.a012", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.29.10.011"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.29.10.011", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t014"], "target_head": "t014"}], "ref": "PSA.29.10", "review_notes": ["The italic *as King* of the first colon is `added`; the written מֶלֶךְ stands later in the verse and cannot be resumed backward under rule 25."], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Hebrew projection", "target_edition": "ASV", "variant_decisions": []}
